url: "https://balouf.github.io/tinto/"
abstract: "How long does a self-stabilizing graph coloring take to settle? Tinto measures it with a Numba-compiled Monte Carlo over pluggable graphs, guards, schedulers and recoloring rules, down to the variance and skewness of the stabilization time. For the conflict-guard rule under the random central daemon, it also provides exact results."
license: MIT
